.TH MDHEAR 1 "October 2026" "mdhear 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdhear \- dictate Markdown: record speech and transcribe it locally with whisper.cpp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdhear
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B mdhear
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I FILE
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B mdhear
.B setup
[\fIMODEL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdhear
records audio from the default microphone (or reads the audio files named on the command line), transcribes it on the local machine using whisper.cpp, and prints the result as Markdown. No audio or text leaves the computer, except during
.BR "mdhear setup" .
.PP
With no
.I FILE
arguments it records: speaking starts immediately; press
.B Enter
to stop. A file named
.B \-
means audio on standard input. Several files are transcribed in order and separated by a blank line.
.PP
Status messages go to standard error and are shown only when it is a terminal (or hidden with
.BR \-q ),
so standard output contains only the Markdown and is safe to redirect or pipe.
.PP
Unless
.B \-\-plain
is given, certain spoken phrases are interpreted as Markdown formatting commands; see
.BR "VOICE COMMANDS" .
.PP
.B mdhear
is the counterpart of
.BR mdspeak (1),
which reads Markdown aloud.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the Markdown to
.I FILE
instead of standard output. An existing file is overwritten. A
.I FILE
of
.B \-
means standard output.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fIMODEL\fR"
Whisper model: a name such as
.BR tiny.en ,
.BR base.en ,
.BR small.en ,
.BR medium.en ,
or a path to a
.B ggml\-*.bin
file. Named models must have been fetched with
.BR "mdhear setup" .
Default:
.BR base.en .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress status messages on standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-completions " SHELL"
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.B elvish
or
.B powershell
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Do not interpret voice commands; output the raw transcript followed by a newline.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SS Subcommands
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fIMODEL\fR]
Clone and build whisper.cpp into
.I ~/.local/share/mdhear
and download
.I MODEL
(default
.BR base.en ).
Requires
.BR git (1),
.BR cmake (1),
a C++ compiler and
.BR curl (1).
The first build takes a few minutes and the base model is about 150 MB. Re-running with a different model name adds that model; existing files are reused.
.SH VOICE COMMANDS
Commands are matched case-insensitively, ignoring punctuation that the speech model inserts around them.
.TP
.B new paragraph
Insert a blank line.
.TP
.B new line
Insert a line break.
.TP
.BI heading " one" "\fR|\fPtwo\fR|\fPthree"
Start a heading (#, ##, ###). The heading runs to the end of the spoken sentence.
.TP
.B bullet
.TQ
.B bullet point
Start a list item (\-). It runs to the end of the sentence.
.TP
.B numbered item
Start a numbered list item (1.). Markdown renderers renumber automatically.
.TP
.B bold " ... " end bold
Wrap the enclosed words in **double asterisks**.
.TP
.B italic " ... " end italic
Wrap the enclosed words in *single asterisks*.
.TP
.B code " ... " end code
Wrap the enclosed words in `backticks`.
.PP
Everything else is passed through as ordinary prose. Because these are ordinary English words, use
.B \-\-plain
when dictating text that legitimately contains phrases such as "new line" or "bullet point".
.PP
Input files may be anything
.BR ffmpeg (1)
can decode: wav, mp3, m4a, ogg, flac, even video.
.SH EXAMPLES
Dictate into a file:
.PP
.RS
.B mdhear \-o notes.md
.RE
.PP
Saying "heading one, Shopping list. Bullet milk. Bullet eggs. New paragraph. Remember the bags." yields:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Shopping list
\- milk
\- eggs

Remember the bags.
.fi
.RE
.PP
Transcribe a recording with higher accuracy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mdhear setup small.en
mdhear \-m small.en \-o meeting.md meeting.m4a
.fi
.RE
.PP
Raw transcript to the clipboard (X11):
.PP
.RS
.B mdhear \-\-plain | xclip \-selection clipboard
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mdhear/whisper.cpp/
Source and build tree; the executable used is
.IR build/bin/whisper\-cli .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mdhear/models/ggml\-NAME.bin
Downloaded Whisper models.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MDHEAR_MODEL
Default for
.BR \-\-model .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
If set, the data directory is
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/mdhear
instead of
.IR ~/.local/share/mdhear .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Any error: model or whisper.cpp not installed, no recorder available, no speech detected, unreadable audio file. Messages are written to standard error as "mdhear: message".
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage (for example an unknown option).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR pw\-record (1)
(PipeWire) or
.BR arecord (1)
(ALSA) for recording;
.BR ffmpeg (1)
when transcribing files.
.SH BUGS AND LIMITATIONS
Linux only; English models and language only. Transcription accuracy depends on the model: small models can mishear words, so proofread the output. Recording has no live level meter, and the whole recording is transcribed after Enter is pressed rather than as you speak.
.PP
Report issues at https://github.com/ogden-marrow/mdspeak/issues.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdspeak (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR pw\-record (1),
.BR arecord (1)
.SH AUTHORS
